{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1195573-combat-question","id":1195573,"title":"Combat question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T18:51:52-07:00","id":1195573,"title":"Combat question","content":"Hey trying to learn the system and had a quick question. When making an attack in combat, what happens if you buy off the defense difficulty with a success but have no extra successes to buy stunts? Is there anything you can do or do you always need one more success to effect your opponent in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:14:30-07:00","id":1195577,"title":"","content":"Ties favor the defender. If you must beat the defender to do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:20:28-07:00","id":1195888,"title":"","content":"I mean I guess that\u2019s effectively true, but the book describes it as a hit if you spend successes Equal to their defense. Even if we assume you just have to accept no effect without a stunt, how does that work with Momentum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:26:49-07:00","id":1195891,"title":"","content":"RAW it doesn't interact with momentum at all because you succeeded in hitting them, you just didn't damage them, but if you wanted to, I guess you could give momentum for it. I don't thing it would break anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:04:54-07:00","id":1196062,"title":"","content":"Well after running our first game last night, I did figure out that hitting with just enough successes to cancel their defense can be useful if you have a 0-success stunt such as &quot;Empty the Clip&quot; and the opponent's armor was already factored into its defense as an antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T10:37:51-07:00","id":1196116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1195573-combat-question?p=1196062#post1196062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well after running our first game last night, I did figure out that hitting with just enough successes to cancel their defense can be useful if you have a 0-success stunt such as &quot;Empty the Clip&quot; and the opponent's armor was already factored into its defense as an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm still reading through the books. Where is this stunt?<br /> <br /> edit: helps if I look in Trinity instead of Scion. D'oh. For posterity, in Scion, this isn't called out as a stunt, and is just an enhancement provided by the automatic tag, but it doesn't automatically make you out of ammo, it just prompts an ammo check, and you explicitly have to apply the enhancement to damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 03-16-2018, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}